Third-party notices

Japanese morphology checks use kuromojin (MIT) and kuromoji (Apache-2.0).
kuromoji bundles the mecab-ipadic-2.7.0-20070801 dictionary data. Its upstream
NOTICE.md requires retention of the NAIST copyright notice and warranty
disclaimer, and also retains the ICOT Free Software no-warranty condition; it
is not identified there as BSD-3-Clause. The upstream notice is available at
https://github.com/takuyaa/kuromoji.js/blob/master/NOTICE.md.

These packages run only in the local analysis-host process. Their dictionary
files are not bundled into the browser build.
